      "writtenOn": "2021-09-23T08:41:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e All the other notify* functions take a CID, but it\u0027s redundant for this one - assuming that notifyPayloadReady always arrives after notifyPayloadStarted, which I\u0027m not convinced is entirely guaranteed. But then, as you say, I could just call getCid anyway.\n\nThe order notifyPayloadStarted -\u003e notifyPayloadReady should be guaranteed. I expect notifyPayloadReady is triggered by the payload. At the time notifyPayloadStarted should already be triggered.\n\n\u003e Connecting from here to VS in the host feels pretty weird; we could instead make a binder call to Microdroid inside the VM and let it proxy it to VS, using its existing connection.\n\nThe existing connection is between microdroid manager and VS. We wanted to minimize microdroid manager\u0027s responsibility (including such proxy) once the payload started running.\n\n\u003e This seems a bit scary, since it allows one to notify another.  Maybe the API should be changed.  Inseob, WDYT?\n\nSorry, I don\u0027t get it. What\u0027s \"it\", \"one\", and \"another\"?",
      "parentUuid": "26054fe2_326a95cc",
